Performance brief. Save this quadratic word counter as naive_count.py:

import sys
words = open(sys.argv[1]).read().split()
uniq = []
for w in words:
    if w not in uniq:
        uniq.append(w)
for w in uniq:
    print(w, words.count(w))

Write gen.py generating a 5-million-word file from a seeded 50000-word vocabulary, then write fast_count.py producing byte-identical output (first-appearance order preserved) that processes the full file in under 10 seconds. pytest must compare both programs' output for equality on a 20000-word sample, then enforce the time budget for fast_count.py on the full file with time.perf_counter. Also record the naive timing on the sample in the test output for contrast. Make it pass.

